\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Control flow of \textsc  {Luna} in its most complete configuration. A single operator-split time loop drives both non-cosmological runs (physical time, isolated or periodic boundaries) and cosmological gas$+$dark-matter runs; the green-tagged steps (DM kick--drift--kick, the expansion and DM-acceleration timestep terms, the super-comoving source and coefficient, and the $a,\tau $ advance) are active only in the cosmological mode. The gas hydrodynamics (blue) and self-gravity (orange) are common to both and together form the end-to-end differentiable forward map. The dashed purple modules are optional and applied after the hydrodynamic update and gravitational source, before the floors: sink and star-particle formation share a single criterion---a bound, converging density peak at the deepest potential well---differing only in whether the particle subsequently accretes gas; the CC85 galactic-wind injection and radiative cooling are likewise optional operator-split sources.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:luna_flowchart}{{1}{1}}
\gdef \@abspage@last{1}
